# What NOT to upload as build context.
#
# Without this file the context is 1.1 GB — .venv alone is 782 MB across 42,033
# files — and `gcloud builds submit` sits there tarring it up with no progress
# output, which looks exactly like a hang.
#
# gcloud will derive this from .gitignore when the file is absent, but only
# after it has already decided how to treat the directory. Being explicit costs
# nothing and removes a variable from a step you will run several times this
# week.

.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# The image builds the SPA itself in stage one. Shipping the host's node_modules
# would upload 40 MB and then be overwritten by `npm ci` anyway.
warden/dashboard/web/node_modules/
warden/dashboard/web/dist/

# Local runtime state and credentials. Neither belongs in a build context, and
# .env in particular would bake a live token into an image layer.
.warden-state/
.env
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
kubeconfig*
service-account*.json

# Terraform state can contain secrets in plaintext.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars

# Docs and planning material are not inputs to the image.
docs/
infra/
tests/
*.md
